# Stage-3 web-parity test build output (scripts/web_parity_test.mjs compiles
# the engine here before running the golden fixtures; never tracked).
/.parity-build/
/.files-build/
# Stage-5 AI suites (scripts/ai_cascade_fixture_test.mjs and
# scripts/ai_injection_test.mjs compile src/lib/ai here via
# scripts/tsconfig.ai.json; rebuildable, never tracked).
/.ai-build/
# Python bytecode cache (update_memory.py / oracle runs; rebuildable, never
# tracked — ADR-018 session, same class as .parity-build).
__pycache__/
# Stage-2 RE tooling (ADR-012 mechanic (a), 2026-11-22): fixtures/re/ is
# THE enumerated synthetic-fixture path — runtime-generated by
# scripts/test_re_tools.py (provenance-headed, program-generated bytes;
# no proprietary content ever). Gitignored by the binding security
# contract, so nothing lands there by accident; committed synthetic
# fixtures (if ever needed) must be text-with-provenance-header only —
# the CI no-binary-blob assertion fails on any binary under fixtures/.
/fixtures/re/
# Only ignore a top-level `/test/` directory (Next.js scaffolding). The
# Flutter app's `clearfile/test/` directory holds real unit and widget
# tests and MUST be tracked.
/test
prompt

server.log
# Skills directory
/skills/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sandbox backup scope (harness/WORKFLOW.md §1 — "Backup scope").
# The event-driven backup (scripts/sandbox_backup.sh) snapshots PROJECT state
# to GitHub. These are sandbox-local scaffolding / user data / big binaries
# and are NEVER backed up to the public repo:
#   .env, db/            - local Prisma config and dev database
#   .zscripts/ Caddyfile tests/ examples/ mini-services/ tool-results/
#                         - platform runtime scaffolding and agent artifacts
#   upload/              - platform drop-zone for user uploads (empty now,
#                          but present on disk; never auto-publish it)
#   download/            - local deliverables (release binaries live on
#                          GitHub Releases; nitro_nissi is an unrelated app)
#   tools/                - SDKs (Flutter toolchain, gitlink)
#   bun.lock              - bun scaffolding re-provisioned by sandbox recycles
#                          (npm/package-lock is the repo standard; see the
#                          2026-11-14 Stage-1 entry session log)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.env
/db/
/.zscripts/
/Caddyfile
/tests/
/examples/
/mini-services/
/tool-results/
/upload/
/download/
/tools/
/bun.lock
# N1 (ADR-017, 2026-11-26 entry gate SEC-1): the Rust core's build
# artifacts must be ignored BEFORE any cargo invocation lands.
/core/target/
# N2 session 1 (the palette generator scratch package — D44): its
# pub/test build artifacts are regenerated, never tracked (the gate
# condition-9 class: the ignore rules land WITH the scaffold, before
# any build — this one landed after the first pub get, out of order;
# the backup blob guard caught the result, as designed).
/scripts/palette_tool/.dart_tool/
/scripts/palette_tool/build/
